# /sdd-evolve

Purpose:
  Evolve the SDD knowledge/skill ecosystem: research current practices,
  compare against existing skills, validate, deduplicate, and deliver
  changes safely. (Git-state sync stays /sdd-update; UPDATE != GIT PULL.)

Owns: commands/sdd-evolve.sdd

Description:
  Runs the Skill Evolution & Update Engine (skills/evolution.sdd):
  loads skill index + metadata (last_verified/review_after), discovers
  new knowledge from official sources (source hierarchy L0-L5) and RIE
  references, compares current vs new, validates against project fit,
  deduplicates (canonical/alias), and produces an Update Manifest with
  safe delivery (direct commit or branch+PR per trust mode).

Usage:
  /sdd-evolve
  /sdd-evolve --deep
  /sdd-evolve @<domain>
  /sdd-evolve --report
  /sdd-evolve --promote

Options:
  --deep     Re-research all critical skills regardless of review_after
  @<domain>  Scope evolution to one domain (e.g. @go, @architecture)
  --report   Show last Update Manifest + evolution status only
  --promote  Evaluate promotion candidates (@project -> @shared)

InitialLoad:
  - skills/evolution.sdd (engine)
  - skills/INDEX.sdd (skill registry routing)
  - .sdd/updates/INDEX.sdd (manifest registry)

Behavior:
  1. LOAD: skill index + per-skill metadata (version, status,
     last_verified, review_after, confidence, depends_on)
  2. DUE: select skills where review_after <= today (or all critical
     with --deep; or @domain scope)
  3. DISCOVER: main repo upstream changes + web research via source
     hierarchy (L0 official first; RIE reference intake if linked)
  4. COMPARE: current guidance vs found practices (SKILL_EVOLUTION
     records with evidence + source level)
  5. VALIDATE: evidence strength, project fit (L0-L5 recommended_for),
     confidence
  6. DEDUP: near-duplicates -> canonical + alias/deprecated
  7. EVOLVE: incremental update (v -> v+1), new child/parent placement,
     promotion candidates, deprecations — SKILL_EVOLUTION record first,
     never direct replacement
  8. VERIFY: SDD consistency check (/sdd-health) + skill tests
     (.sdd/testing run.ps1 knowledge category)
  9. MANIFEST: write .sdd/updates/UPD-<n> (trigger, counts, changes,
     sources, validation result, delivery mode)
  10. DELIVER: own repo -> commit/push; non-collaborator ->
      branch sdd/update/<area>/<slug> + commit sdd(skill): ... + PR
      (PR body: Why/Changes/Sources/Validation/Risk; every change
      carries SOURCE+EVIDENCE+REASON+CHANGE)
  11. REPORT: final counts summary; append prompt-pair ([R104])

AutoMode:
  trigger: none (explicit human command only — evolution research is
  deliberate, not background)
  fail: open (manifest records failure; skills unchanged)

Output:
  SDD EVOLVE COMPLETE
    Sources checked: N (official: X, community: Y)
    Skills checked: N
    Skills unchanged: N
    Skills updated: N
    New skills: N (child: N, standalone: N)
    Deprecated: N
    Deduplicated: N (canonical: <list>)
    References added: N
    Architecture rules changed: N
    Validation: PASSED | FAILED
    Delivery: direct commit <hash> | PR #<n>

Rules:
  [EVO-01] /sdd-evolve NEVER replaces a skill directly — every change
           starts as a SKILL_EVOLUTION record (evidence-backed).
  [EVO-02] Source hierarchy L0>L1>L2>L3>L4>L5 governs confidence;
           L5-only (AI inference) changes are proposals, never updates.
  [EVO-03] Skills past review_after are re-researched; fresh skills
           are skipped (unless --deep).
  [EVO-04] Deduplication runs before creation: canonical is chosen,
           duplicates become aliases/references/deprecated — [SK13]
           granularity, [R81] link over copy.
  [EVO-05] Delivery respects trust mode: TRUST_0..TRUST_5 map to
           Phase 131 authority levels; direct push requires L4-style
           human approval for irreversible registry changes.
  [EVO-06] Update Manifest (UPD-<n>) is mandatory for every run —
           machine-readable audit trail ([R95] references it).
  [EVO-07] NO_VALUE research outcome -> DISCARD (research does not
           obligate skill creation) — recorded in research record.
  [EVO-08] Routing files touched by evolution stay human-authored
           ([R109]); evolution PROPOSES routing edits, never rewrites.

Mode: SUPERVISED

Navigation:
  INDEX: @../../INDEX.sdd
  Engine: @../skills/evolution.sdd
  Updates: @../updates/INDEX.sdd
  RIE: @../references/engine.sdd

